WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:02.940
Now, that you've seen
the WeatherEntry class for

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.560
the weather table, it's your turn.

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:06.860
Add the constants for

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:11.850
the location table in the LocationEntry
inner contract class.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:16.200
These constants included the table name,
and the name of each column.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.950
As we've shown in a few previous
diagrams, the columns need to store

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:25.010
the location setting, latitude,
longitude, and the city name.

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.720
After you finish coding
the location entry class,

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.190
make sure to look at the solution video.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:33.760
You'll want to use the same constant
names that we use, since the code in

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.280
the other classes you received relies
on these constant names being the same.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.148
Once you've finished,

00:00:39.148 --> 00:00:43.000
you will have defined all of
the columns for both of the tables.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.300
Next, we'll be ready to use these column
names to actually create the tables

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:47.850
in the database.

